From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: Let the compositor drag data to clients

A drag that starts on a compositor actor never reached a client: only a
client's wl_data_source could start a Wayland drag, so files shown by the
Shell could not be dropped anywhere but the Shell.

MetaDataDrag is a compositor-owned drag source. It offers MIME types with
content given up front or later, and starts the regular Wayland drag grab
from the press or motion of a pointer button or touch point. Wayland clients
get a wl_data_offer; X11 clients get the drag through the XDND bridge, which
reads the DND selection as for any Wayland drag. Over something that is not
a client surface, "motion" returns the action a compositor drop would
perform (shown by the cursor) and "drop" lets the compositor take it.
"ended" reports how the grab ended and "finished" when the content is no
longer offered. With no modifier held a target gets the preferred action;
Shift and Control choose move and copy as before. A cancelled touch point
cancels the drag.

The drag grab now accepts a drag without an origin surface.
---
diff --git a/src/meson.build b/src/meson.build
index 118cbe386..9ca496c80 100644
--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -527,6 +527,8 @@ mutter_sources += [
   'wayland/meta-pointer-confinement-wayland.h',
   'wayland/meta-pointer-lock-wayland.c',
   'wayland/meta-pointer-lock-wayland.h',
+  'wayland/meta-data-drag.c',
+  'wayland/meta-data-drag-private.h',
   'wayland/meta-selection-source-wayland.c',
   'wayland/meta-selection-source-wayland-private.h',
   'wayland/meta-wayland-activation.c',
